      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "${(\\frac{s}{2})}^{4}{(\\frac{4}{t})}^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We apply the power of quotient rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{s}{2})}^{4}{(\\frac{4}{t})}^{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{{s}^{4}}{{2}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{{4}^{2}}{{t}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{s}^{4}}{16}\\cdot \\frac{16}{{t}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{16{s}^{4}}{16{t}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{s}^{4}}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
