    "q-72638": {
      "dom_id": "step-q72638",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "${(\\frac{3}{4x})}^{2}{(\\frac{-2x}{5})}^{3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the power of quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3}{4x})}^{2}{(\\frac{-2x}{5})}^{3}=\\frac{{3}^{2}}{(4x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{(-2x)^{3}}{{5}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we apply the power of product rule and multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{3}^{2}}{(4x)^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{(-2x)^{3}}{{5}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{3}^{2}}{{4}^{2}{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{(-2)^{3}{x}^{3}}{{5}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{9}{16{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{-8{x}^{3}}{125} & = \\\\ \\frac{-8\\cdot 9{x}^{3}}{16\\cdot 125{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we apply the quotient rule and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-8\\cdot 9{x}^{3}}{16\\cdot 125{x}^{2}} & = \\\\ -\\frac{9{x}^{3-2}}{2\\cdot 125} & = \\\\ -\\frac{9x}{250}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
